  pm-gh1605,related,"2026-11-01T12:19:05.401Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-01T21:06:24.581Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause: buildInvalidArgumentGuidance classified any message containing \" must be \" or \" requires \" as invalid_argument_value, and applyPmCliErrorContext only replaced the generic title for command_failed. The likely_duplicate refusal interpolates candidate item titles into its message, so a duplicate whose title contains either phrase was classified as a bad flag value. It got the \"Invalid argument value\" headline and the misleading \"Check allowed values in command help\" next step.\n\nFix (src/cli/error-guidance.ts): substring heuristics now classify only untyped text. A typed code keeps the invalid-argument route only when its message starts with \"Invalid \" or it declares an allowed domain. Whenever a typed code overrides a generic class (command_failed or invalid_argument_value), the headline is the message's first line. JSON title and code agree, and generic-coded refusals keep the class title.\n\nNegative control: the published 2026.11.1 tarball's dist/cli/error-guidance.js returns title \"Invalid argument value\" plus the \"Check allowed values\" step for the same input. The new case in tests/unit/cli/error-guidance.spec.ts asserts the typed first-line headline in JSON, in classification and on the first line of the human output.\n"
files[2]{path,scope}:
  src/cli/error-guidance.ts,project
  tests/unit/cli/error-guidance.spec.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/cli/error-guidance.spec.ts,project,600,"harness:claude-code","2026-11-01T20:27:10.287Z",local_mutation,fix/refusal-contract-precision
close_reason: Typed refusals keep their own headline when interpolated data resembles a validation message
escape_class: production_defect
